this research question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nReturn five non-overlapping investigation tracks tailored to the subject. Each track needs a short display label, a search query, and a sentence explaining what evidence it should seek. Favor complementary evidence needs and avoid restating the same query. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:55:38.569918Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://58d07cdf-5045-7102-845c-0289da94770e","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"angles":[{"focus":"Find authoritative listings of available skills, their publishers, and official curation or featured status to establish the candidate pool.","label":"Official catalog & marketplaces","query":"Muse Code skills catalog marketplace best SKILL.md 2024 2025"},{"focus":"Gather community evidence of quality such as stars, download counts, user reviews, and curated awesome-lists to rank candidates.","label":"Quality signals & reviews","query":"best Muse skills reviews stars downloads community recommendations"},{"focus":"Identify structural traits of high-quality skills including clear triggers, scoped instructions, examples, and maintainability to use as an evaluation rubric.","label":"Skill anatomy & quality criteria","query":"what makes a good SKILL.md structure frontmatter instructions examples"},{"focus":"Collect evidence on risks and vetting steps such as permission scope, script execution, and provenance checks before installation.","label":"Safety & trust vetting","query":"Muse skill security audit prompt injection malicious skills vetting checklist"},{"focus":"Map skills by task domain to spot complementary options and coverage gaps so the eventual pick fills an unmet workflow need.","label":"Domain coverage & gaps","query":"Claude Code skills by category coding testing docs git browser 3D"}]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1652e-dbac-7471-a0a2-d297ecfcd1b7","turnId":"01a1652e-b798-7410-91e1-e14b341831f9","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":0,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":0,"inputTokens":21902,"outputTokens":482,"reasoningTokens":120},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1652ebd5b774282f936b33921cd01"},"opened_ordinal":34,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1651f-704c-7823-be7c-491b20d3e2c1","sequence":253},"last":{"id":"01a1652e-f4c9-7111-8fcf-e519e2e3b706","sequence":267},"stream_id":"01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1652e-f539-7110-ac58-f87002fe2026":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/2","childSessionId":"ee5f0f16-025a-7f83-8562-08cfc48639fb","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":15577,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Muse Code skills catalog marketplace best SKILL.md 2024 2025\nEvidence goal: Find authoritative listings of available skills, their publishers, and official curation or featured status to establish the candidate pool.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","itemId":"9aa46379-f4b6-556d-83ef-6ff470c5444d","kind":"subagent","objective":"Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Muse Code skills catalog marketplace best SKILL.md 2024 2025\nEvidence goal: Find authoritative listings of available skills, their publishers, and official curation or featured status to establish the candidate pool.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:55:54.737512Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://fdb7dbb8-725a-7f83-89cd-6f558b61a3c7","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"claims":[{"claim":"Largest community catalog for Muse is aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills with 2,384 curated, safety-reviewed, free skills using open Agent Skills SKILL.md format","evidence":[{"excerpt":"A community catalog of 2,384 agent skills for Meta's Muse personal assistant — curated, safety-reviewed, and free to use.","source_url":"https://github.com/aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills"},{"excerpt":"Skills use the open Agent Skills format — YAML frontmatter (`name` + `description`) followed by markdown instructions — so the same skill works across assistants that support the format, including Meta's Muse.","source_url":"https://github.com/aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Meta Muse has no official skill-install flow; skills are used by opening SKILL.md and pasting into chat, while Muse Code reads standard SKILL.md files","evidence":[{"excerpt":"No installers, no packages. Meta's Muse doesn't have an official skill-install flow","source_url":"https://github.com/aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills"},{"excerpt":"Meta has said more of its own Skills are coming to Muse but has not announced a way to upload yours; Muse Code, its developer tool, already reads standard SKILL.md files, so these files are ready if uplo","source_url":"https://www.aiagentslibrary.com/skills/meta-muse/"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Agensi is the largest commercial Muse skills marketplace with 13,227 live skills across 32 use cases, ranked by installs and reviews, mostly paid one-time purchase","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Currently 13,227 live skills for Muse, across 32 use cases, with new listings published every week.","source_url":"https://www.agensi.io/muse-marketplace"},{"excerpt":"Some skills are free, but most are paid. Paid skills show the price upfront, are a one-time purchase, and include future updates from the creator.","source_url":"https://www.agensi.io/muse-marketplace"},{"excerpt":"Every category is a dedicated Muse page with its own inventory, ranked by installs and reviews.","source_url":"https://www.agensi.io/muse-marketplace"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Agensi marketplace scale validated independently: crossed 2,000 skills, 3,000 users, 50,000 monthly visitors three months after launch in July 2026 with 200+ creators","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Agensi, the skill store for AI agents, has crossed 2,000 skills, 3,000 registered users, and 50,000 monthly visitors three months after launch. The marketplace, powered by a community of more than 200 expert creators","source_url":"http://www.newsfilecorp.com/release/304200/Agensi-Crosses-2000-Skills-Three-Months-After-Launching-Its-AI-Agent-Marketplace"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Muse Code ships 20 bundled built-in skills verifiable via `muse skills list --source built-in`","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Twenty bundled skills, and four of them are for leaving ... `muse skills list --source built-in` returns twenty entries.","source_url":"https://dev.to/yuan2080/muse-code-bundles-20-skills-and-4-move-you-off-claude-code-3944"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Official bundled skill IDs include create-skill, doctor, git, grill, import, manage-settings, plan, read-session and taste","evidence":[{"excerpt":"The real built-in skill ids are `create-skill`, `doctor`, `git`, `grill`, `grill-and-record`, `import`, `manage-settings`, `plan`, `read-session` and `taste`.","source_url":"https://codersera.com/blog/how-to-install-muse-code-cli-2026/"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Core featured bundled skills are /plan (approval-gated plan), /grill (stress-tests plan) and /goal (works toward objective)","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Muse Code ships with several default skills. `/plan` turns a task into an approval-gated plan, `/grill` stress-tests that plan until it holds up, and `/goal` works toward successful completion of the specified objective.","source_url":"https://newswings.com.ng/introducing-muse-code-and-muse-spark-1-2/"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Community collection rallat/muse-skills provides 53 workflow skills each with SKILL.md plus references/scripts","evidence":[{"excerpt":"53 skills — each directory holds `SKILL.md` (the skill's instructions) plus supporting references and scripts. These are workflow skills (documents, email-management, flight-booking, shopping, …).","source_url":"https://github.com/rallat/muse-skills"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"No single official Meta-curated featured marketplace for Muse Code was found; candidate pool splits into bundled built-ins, Agensi commercial marketplace, and GitHub community catalogs","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Skills are plain SKILL.md files, so the same skill you use with Muse also runs in Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI and 20+ other agents.","source_url":"https://www.agensi.io/muse-marketplace"}],"importance":"edge_case"}],"sources":[{"published_at":"2026-01-01","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"GitHub - aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills: A community catalog of 2,384 agent skills for Meta's Muse","url":"https://github.com/aicodedecode/awesome-muse-skills"},{"published_at":"2026-01-01","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Muse Skills Marketplace - Browse 13,000+ Skills - Agensi","url":"https://www.agensi.io/muse-marketplace"},{"published_at":"2026-10-26","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Muse Code bundles 20 skills, and 4 move you off Claude Code - DEV","url":"https://dev.to/yuan2080/muse-code-bundles-20-skills-and-4-move-you-off-claude-code-3944"},{"published_at":"2026-08-10","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to Install Muse Code CLI (2026 Setup Guide) - Codersera","url":"https://codersera.com/blog/how-to-install-muse-code-cli-2026/"},{"published_at":"2026-07-28","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Introducing Muse Code and Muse Spark 1.2 - NewsWings","url":"https://newswings.com.ng/introducing-muse-code-and-muse-spark-1-2/"},{"published_at":"2026-07-09","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Agensi Crosses 2,000 Skills Three Months After Launching Its AI Agent Marketplace - Newsfile","url":"http://www.newsfilecorp.com/release/304200/Agensi-Crosses-2000-Skills-Three-Months-After-Launching-Its-AI-Agent-Marketplace"},{"published_at":"2026-01-01","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"GitHub - rallat/muse-skills: skills from muse","url":"https://github.com/rallat/muse-skills"},{"published_at":"2026-10-10","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Free Meta Muse Skills: Download or Copy (2026) - AI Agents Library","url":"https://www.aiagentslibrary.com/skills/meta-muse/"}]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1652e-f539-7110-ac58-f87002fe2026","turnId":"01a1652e-b798-7410-91e1-e14b341831f9","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":45672,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":45672,"inputTokens":73485,"outputTokens":2423,"reasoningTokens":240},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1652ebd5b774282f936b33921cd01"},"opened_ordinal":45,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1651f-704c-7d74-856a-3f6bb2572c01","sequence":274},"last":{"id":"01a1652f-33f1-7db0-9a82-cd313a9e7843","sequence":344},"stream_id":"01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1652e-f623-7363-a56a-4992798f0055":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/3","childSessionId":"ee5f0e16-025a-7dd0-8562-07cfc4863848","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":31815,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: best Muse skills reviews stars downloads community recommendations\nEvidence goal: Gather community evidence of quality such as stars, download counts, user reviews, and curated awesome-lists to rank candidates.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","itemId":"a2258b9d-52d2-5c5e-b384-f722f131d140","kind":"subagent","objective":"Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: best Muse skills reviews stars downloads community recommendations\nEvidence goal: Gather community evidence of quality such as stars, download counts, user reviews, and curated awesome-lists to rank candidates.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:56:11.33211Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://fdb7dab8-725a-7dd0-89cd-6e558b61a214","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"claims":[{"claim":"Rank 1 by stars/installs: obra/superpowers is the most-endorsed skill pack - 293,000+ GitHub stars (Sep 2026) and the top recommendation for engineering discipline.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"The best Claude Code skills in 2026 are Superpowers (293,000+ GitHub stars), Anthropic's official skills repo (Skill Creator + document skills), gstack, and GSD.","source_url":"https://www.taskade.com/blog/claude-code-skills"},{"excerpt":"| 1 | Superpowers | Engineering discipline end to end | obra/superpowers (293K+) |","source_url":"https://www.taskade.com/blog/claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Superpowers also leads on installs: passed 750,000 installs in the Claude plugin directory by June 2026, second only to Anthropic's frontend design plugin, with almost 27,000 forks and an official Anthropic marketplace spot.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"It has almost 27,000 forks, an official spot in Anthropic’s plugin marketplace, and by June it had passed 750,000 installs in the Claude plugin directory, second only to Anthropic’s own frontend design plugin.","source_url":"https://medium.com/@itaispector1/everyone-says-to-install-this-claude-code-plugin-it-only-beat-claude-at-2-things-superpowers-8a5730fada92"},{"excerpt":"A repository made mostly of markdown files just passed 300,000 stars on GitHub.","source_url":"https://medium.com/@itaispector1/everyone-says-to-install-this-claude-code-plugin-it-only-beat-claude-at-2-things-superpowers-8a5730fada92"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Rank 2 / safest first install: anthropics/skills (Anthropic official) had about 179,000 stars on Sep 29 2026 and holds Skill Creator, document skills, mcp-builder and webapp-testing; Taskade recommends starting there.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Start with Anthropic's official anthropics/skills repository, which had about 179,000 stars on September 29, 2026 and holds Skill Creator, the document skills, mcp-builder, webapp-testing, and","source_url":"https://www.taskade.com/blog/claude-code-skills"},{"excerpt":"| 2 | Skill Creator | Building your own skills | anthropics/skills (179K+) |","source_url":"https://www.taskade.com/blog/claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Independent corroboration of anthropics/skills scale: GitHub reports 178,887 stars and 21,147 forks as of 2026-09-29, 19 skill folders at HEAD, and skill-creator shows 374,263 all-time installs as of Sep 7 2026 sync.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"GitHub reports 178,887 stars and 21,147 forks on anthropics/skills as of 2026-09-29 (GitHub API).","source_url":"https://medium.com/@skillselion/why-your-claude-code-skill-never-triggers-according-to-anthropics-skill-creator-1c25850309c3"},{"excerpt":"The skill-creator listing shows 374,263 all-time installs as of the September 7, 2026 sync of the Skillselion catalog (checked 2026-09-29).","source_url":"https://medium.com/@skillselion/why-your-claude-code-skill-never-triggers-according-to-anthropics-skill-creator-1c25850309c3"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Best curated discovery list by stars: ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills has 77,644 GitHub stars per SkillsLLM (other roundups cite ~67k, showing counts rise quickly / vary by date).","evidence":[{"excerpt":"It has 77,644 GitHub stars.","source_url":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/composiohq-awesome-claude-skills"},{"excerpt":"The largest are ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills (~67k stars) and travisvn/awesome-claude-skills (~14k stars), plus alirezarezvani/claude-skills, which bundles hundreds of skills, agents, and commands.","source_url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Other curated awesome-lists for discovery: travisvn/awesome-claude-skills ~8.1k stars with an Individual Skills section, VoltAgent/awesome-agent-skills ~9.1k with 500+ skills, and hesreallyhim/awesome-claude-code ~26.1k (56,158 in a later AY Automate table) with an Agent Skills category.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"| **awesome-claude-code** | ~26.1k | Has \"Agent Skills\" category | `hesreallyhim/awesome-claude-code` |","source_url":"https://gist.github.com/zoharbabin/cf5ab80b2b0af50e34328b5eb2bfdc93"},{"excerpt":"| **awesome-claude-skills** | ~8.1k | Has \"Individual Skills\" section | `travisvn/awesome-claude-skills` |","source_url":"https://gist.github.com/zoharbabin/cf5ab80b2b0af50e34328b5eb2bfdc93"},{"excerpt":"| awesome-claude-code | Curated directory of skills, hooks, plugins, and resources | 56,158 | Directory |","source_url":"https://www.ayautomate.com/blog/best-claude-code-github-repos"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Safety signal for ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills: SkillsLLM says it passed an automated security scan (dependency vulnerability audit plus prompt-injection heuristics) with no high-severity issues - automated only, not a human review guarantee.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"A: Yes. awesome-claude-skills passed SkillsLLM's automated security scan — a dependency vulnerability audit plus prompt-injection heuristics — with no high-severity issues.","source_url":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/composiohq-awesome-claude-skills"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Community consensus shortlist beyond stars: superpowers for plan-first TDD, Anthropic frontend-design for UI, official document skills (pdf, docx, xlsx, pptx) for files, a Playwright testing skill, security-review, and one design layer.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"The short list most developers converge on: superpowers for plan-first TDD, Anthropic's free frontend-design skill for UI, the official document skills (pdf, docx, xlsx, pptx) for files, a Playwright testing skill so Claude can verify what it built, security-review before you ship, and one design layer so your UI does not look generic.","source_url":"https://superdesign.dev/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Caveat for this Muse Code context: Muse Code has no third-party plugin ecosystem, marketplace or community catalogue yet, unlike Claude Code; its bundled skills are /plan, /grilling, /grill-with-docs and /taste. Claude-ecosystem star rankings therefore do not directly imply Muse installability.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"No third-party plugin ecosystem, no marketplace, no community catalogue.","source_url":"https://composio.dev/content/muse-code-vs-claude-code"},{"excerpt":"The bundled skills are `/plan` (turns a task into an approval-gated, decision-complete plan), `/grilling` (stress-tests a plan until it holds), `/grill-with-docs` (same, but records decisions into project docs), and `/taste` (a design-quality gate for frontend work).","source_url":"https://composio.dev/content/muse-code-vs-claude-code"}],"importance":"edge_case"},{"claim":"Muse-native discovery is nascent: Skill Harbor is described as an open directory/marketplace of AI skills for Meta's Muse with copy-paste install prompts, and the only GitHub muse-skills repo found (rallat/muse-skills) has just 1 star and 0 watchers - no comparable star/download evidence exists yet for Muse-native skills.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Skill Harbor is an open directory and marketplace of AI skills for Meta's Muse. Sellers publish skills (free or paid) with copy-paste install prompts, so anyone can extend their Muse in seconds.","source_url":"https://shipwithmuse.live/builds/muse-spark-1-3-inside-box-ai"},{"excerpt":"- **Stars:** 1\n- **Watchers:** 0","source_url":"https://github.com/rallat/muse-skills"}],"importance":"edge_case"}],"sources":[{"published_at":"2026-09-29 (Updated September 29, 2026 per page)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Best Claude Code Skills in 2026 (Tested + How to Build) - Taskade","url":"https://www.taskade.com/blog/claude-code-skills"},{"published_at":"2026 (page_last_modified 1792540800, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Everyone Says to Install This Claude Code Plugin. It Only Beat Claude at 2 Things (Superpowers) - Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@itaispector1/everyone-says-to-install-this-claude-code-plugin-it-only-beat-claude-at-2-things-superpowers-8a5730fada92"},{"published_at":"unknown (accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"awesome-claude-skills - AI Agents on GitHub (77.6k stars) | SkillsLLM","url":"https://skillsllm.com/skill/composiohq-awesome-claude-skills"},{"published_at":"2026 (page_last_modified 1783382400, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Best Claude Code Skills (2026): 15 Tested & Ranked - DesignRevision","url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"},{"published_at":"unknown (accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Agent Skills Ecosystem: Distribution & Discovery Guide - GitHub Gist","url":"https://gist.github.com/zoharbabin/cf5ab80b2b0af50e34328b5eb2bfdc93"},{"published_at":"2026 (page_last_modified 1792540800, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Claude Code GitHub Repos: 12 Best to Install (2026) - AY Automate","url":"https://www.ayautomate.com/blog/best-claude-code-github-repos"},{"published_at":"2026-09-29 data check (page_last_modified 1790640000, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Why Your Claude Code Skill Never Triggers, According to Anthropic's skill-creator - Medium/Skillselion","url":"https://medium.com/@skillselion/why-your-claude-code-skill-never-triggers-according-to-anthropics-skill-creator-1c25850309c3"},{"published_at":"2026 (page_last_modified 1786492800, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Muse Code vs Claude Code: Should you switch? - Composio","url":"https://composio.dev/content/muse-code-vs-claude-code"},{"published_at":"2026 (page_last_modified 1790294400, accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Muse Spark 1.3 inside Box AI / Skill Harbor - ShipWithMuse","url":"https://shipwithmuse.live/builds/muse-spark-1-3-inside-box-ai"},{"published_at":"unknown (accessed 2026-10-22)","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"GitHub - rallat/muse-skills: skills from muse","url":"https://github.com/rallat/muse-skills"}]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1652e-f623-7363-a56a-4992798f0055","turnId":"01a1652e-b798-7410-91e1-e14b341831f9","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":73948,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":73948,"inputTokens":107277,"outputTokens":4332,"reasoningTokens":717},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1652ebd5b774282f936b33921cd01"},"opened_ordinal":51,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1651f-704c-7253-8a56-2676e860b582","sequence":288},"last":{"id":"01a1652f-74c4-7732-be47-f6dd767200e3","sequence":365},"stream_id":"01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1652e-f75b-7bb3-ac47-d693c349e9c6":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/4","childSessionId":"ee5f1516-025b-79b5-8562-0ecfc486442d","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":78741,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: what makes a good SKILL.md structure frontmatter instructions examples\nEvidence goal: Identify structural traits of high-quality skills including clear triggers, scoped instructions, examples, and maintainability to use as an evaluation rubric.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","itemId":"76b68134-ad87-5ff7-bb15-ee107e9ea933","kind":"subagent","objective":"Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: what makes a good SKILL.md structure frontmatter instructions examples\nEvidence goal: Identify structural traits of high-quality skills including clear triggers, scoped instructions, examples, and maintainability to use as an evaluation rubric.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:56:58.591574Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://fdb7e1b8-725b-79b5-89cd-6d558b61a061","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"claims":[{"claim":"Every SKILL.md requires YAML frontmatter with required fields name and description; this is the mandatory structural baseline for evaluation.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Every Skill requires a `SKILL.md` file with YAML frontmatter: **Required fields:** `name` and `description`","source_url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"The name must be a lowercase hyphenated identifier matching the skill directory name (kebab-case, no underscores/spaces/uppercase).","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Must match the skill’s directory name","source_url":"https://claude.com/docs/skills/how-to"},{"excerpt":"Use descriptive names: The `name` field should be kebab-case and match the skill directory name","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills/7.2-configuration-files"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"The description is the trigger mechanism: it must state what the skill does AND when to use it, because the agent reads it to decide whether to load the skill.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"What the skill does and when to use it. ... Claude reads this to decide when to load the skill. Up to 1,024 characters, the limit in the Agent Skills specification","source_url":"https://claude.com/docs/skills/how-to"},{"excerpt":"Description contains explicit positive triggers (what should activate the skill)","source_url":"https://www.mtechzilla.com/blogs/how-to-develop-skill-md-production-guide-engineering-teams"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"High-quality descriptions include explicit trigger phrases / 'Use when...' conditions with natural language phrases users might say, not just a generic summary.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Include trigger phrases: The `description` field should contain natural language phrases that users might say (e.g., \"Deploy my app\", \"Check performance\")","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills/7.2-configuration-files"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Skills use progressive disclosure: only name+description load at startup (~100 tokens), the full SKILL.md body loads on trigger (<5k tokens recommended), and referenced files load only on demand.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Only the name and description load at session start; the full body loads when Claude invokes the skill","source_url":"https://claude.com/resources/articles/steering-claude-code-skills-hooks-rules-subagents-and-more"},{"excerpt":"| **Level 1: Metadata** | `name` + `description` from frontmatter | ~100 tokens per skill | Always (for all skills) |","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/supabase/agent-skills/2.2-agent-skills-open-standard"},{"excerpt":"| **Level 2: Body** | Full `SKILL.md` markdown body | <5k tokens (recommended) | When description matches context |","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/supabase/agent-skills/2.2-agent-skills-open-standard"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Maintainability requires keeping SKILL.md concise (under 500 lines) and moving detailed reference material to separate bundled files loaded only when needed.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"`SKILL.md` is under 500 lines","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/tech-leads-club/agent-skills/7.2-skill-writing-guidelines"},{"excerpt":"**keep SKILL.md under 500 lines** and move detailed reference material into separate files in the skill directory","source_url":"https://dev.to/rulestack/skillmd-how-to-write-a-claude-code-skill-that-actually-triggers-format-template-27cp"},{"excerpt":"`SKILL.md`: Main instructions (loaded when triggered)","source_url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/best-practices"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Bundled supporting files (reference, examples, forms) should be separated so they load as needed rather than bloating the main instructions.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"`FORMS.md`: Form-filling guide (loaded as needed)","source_url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/best-practices"},{"excerpt":"If Claude determines a skill is needed, it reads the full SKILL.md file. For additional detail, skills can include a references/ directory with supporting documentation loaded only on demand.","source_url":"https://claude.com/resources/articles/building-agents-with-skills-equipping-agents-for-specialized-work"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Instructions should be written in imperative form ('Do X', not 'You should X') with sequentially numbered steps.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"All instructions are written in imperative form (`Do X`, not `You should X`)","source_url":"https://www.mtechzilla.com/blogs/how-to-develop-skill-md-production-guide-engineering-teams"},{"excerpt":"Instructions are in imperative mood","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/tech-leads-club/agent-skills/7.2-skill-writing-guidelines"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"High-quality skills include concrete examples showing input to output rather than verbose abstract explanation.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Examples show concrete input → output","source_url":"https://deepwiki.com/tech-leads-club/agent-skills/7.2-skill-writing-guidelines"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Description length is capped at 1,024 characters per the Agent Skills specification, so triggers must be concise and specific.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Claude reads this to decide when to load the skill. Up to 1,024 characters, the limit in the Agent Skills specification","source_url":"https://claude.com/docs/skills/how-to"}],"importance":"edge_case"}],"sources":[{"published_at":"unknown","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Agent Skills - Claude Platform Docs (Overview)","url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview"},{"published_at":"2026-09-28","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Create custom skills - Claude Docs","url":"https://claude.com/docs/skills/how-to"},{"published_at":"unknown","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Skill authoring best practices - Claude Platform Docs","url":"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/best-practices"},{"published_at":"2026-06-17","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Steering Claude Code: when to use CLAUDE.md, skills, hooks, and subagents","url":"https://claude.com/resources/articles/steering-claude-code-skills-hooks-rules-subagents-and-more"},{"published_at":"2026-01-22","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Building agents with Skills: Equipping agents for specialized work","url":"https://claude.com/resources/articles/building-agents-with-skills-equipping-agents-for-specialized-work"},{"published_at":"2026-02-10","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Agent Skills Open Standard - Supabase","url":"https://deepwiki.com/supabase/agent-skills/2.2-agent-skills-open-standard"},{"published_at":"2026-02-02","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Skill Writing Guidelines - tech-leads-club/agent-skills","url":"https://deepwiki.com/tech-leads-club/agent-skills/7.2-skill-writing-guidelines"},{"published_at":"2026-07-21","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to Develop SKILL.md for AI Coding Agents - MTechZilla production guide","url":"https://www.mtechzilla.com/blogs/how-to-develop-skill-md-production-guide-engineering-teams"},{"published_at":"2026-01-24","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Configuration Files - vercel-labs/agent-skills","url":"https://deepwiki.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills/7.2-configuration-files"},{"published_at":"2026-11-04","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"SKILL.md: how to write a Claude Code skill that actually triggers (format + template)","url":"https://dev.to/rulestack/skillmd-how-to-write-a-claude-code-skill-that-actually-triggers-format-template-27cp"}]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1652e-f75b-7bb3-ac47-d693c349e9c6","turnId":"01a1652e-b798-7410-91e1-e14b341831f9","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":136516,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":136516,"inputTokens":167969,"outputTokens":5427,"reasoningTokens":2149},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1652ebd5b774282f936b33921cd01"},"opened_ordinal":57,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1651f-704c-778b-8bc2-7ee63f7052c0","sequence":302},"last":{"id":"01a16530-2d5f-7a63-a5d1-24ec25608ca3","sequence":372},"stream_id":"01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1652e-f8a2-7043-b866-9200c7f53411":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/5","childSessionId":"ee5f1416-025b-7802-8562-0dcfc486427a","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":21041,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Muse skill security audit prompt injection malicious skills vetting checklist\nEvidence goal: Collect evidence on risks and vetting steps such as permission scope, script execution, and provenance checks before installation.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","itemId":"4a374067-2e3d-51a5-8420-152253ce6bbb","kind":"subagent","objective":"Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Muse skill security audit prompt injection malicious skills vetting checklist\nEvidence goal: Collect evidence on risks and vetting steps such as permission scope, script execution, and provenance checks before installation.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:56:01.256355Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://fdb7e0b8-725b-7802-89cd-6c558b619eae","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"claims":[{"claim":"91% of confirmed malicious skills use prompt injection as their primary attack vector, so SKILL.md must be read line-by-line for role-override language and hidden instructions.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Detect prompt injection indicators.** Read the SKILL.md line by line, looking for role-override language (\"ignore previous instructions\", \"you are now\", \"override your guidelines\"), hidden instructions in HTML comments or zero-width Unicode characters, and any text that attempts to redirect agent behaviour. 91% of confirmed malicious skills use prompt injection as their primary attack vector (Snyk, \"SKILL.md to Shell Access\").","source_url":"https://automationswitch.com/ai-workflows/agent-skills-security-audit-guide-how-to-verify-skill-md-files-before-you-install"},{"excerpt":"also shows an evolution in agent attacks: 100% of confirmed malicious skills contain malicious code patterns, while 91% simultaneously employ prompt injection techniques.","source_url":"https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan/raw/d57a0ca538a8cabb5c3bbc3c9e992fc828f97ba4/.github/reports/skills-report.pdf"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Prompt injection is combined with traditional malicious code: injections prime the agent to accept code a human would reject, while code achieves objectives prompt manipulation alone cannot.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"This combination of promptbased attacks and malicious software can be highly effective: injections prime the agent to accept malicious code, which a human would normally reject, while the code accomplishes objectives that prompt manipulation alone cannot","source_url":"https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan/raw/d57a0ca538a8cabb5c3bbc3c9e992fc828f97ba4/.github/reports/skills-report.pdf"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"In February 2026 Snyk scanned 3,984 skills: 36.82% (1,467) had at least one security flaw, 13.4% (534) a critical issue, and 76 were confirmed malicious.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"In February 2026, Snyk scanned 3,984 skills across the ClawHub and skills.sh marketplaces. The result: 36.82% of them, 1,467 skills, carry at least one security flaw, and 13.4%, 534 skills, contain a critical-level issue.","source_url":"https://enapragma.co/field-notes/agent-skills-are-untrusted-code"},{"excerpt":"Snyk scanned 3,984 skills on ClawHub and found 1,467 (36.82%) had at least one security flaw, 534 (13.4%) contained critical-level issues (malware distribution, prompt injection, or exposed secrets), and 76 were confirmed malicious.","source_url":"https://guard0.ai/blog/ai-agent-supply-chain-security"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"A skill is both instructions the agent will obey and optional scripts it will run with the user's permissions, so it must be treated as untrusted software/dependency.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"A skill is two things at once: a SKILL.md file your agent will obey, and optional scripts your agent will run with your permissions. That makes a skill software, and it deserves the same suspicion you give any dependency.","source_url":"https://dev.to/plastikelectrik/your-ai-agent-obeys-any-skill-you-install-i-built-an-auditor-to-check-them-first-4a2o"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Skills are not verified by the platform and may contain prompt injections, hidden instructions, or malicious scripts; always inspect before installation.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"\"Skills are not verified by GitHub and may contain prompt injections, hidden instructions, or malicious scripts. Always inspect the content of a skill before installation using `gh skill pre","source_url":"https://dev.to/gde/auditing-agent-skills-a-threat-model-for-the-next-generation-of-ai-package-managers-2g25"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Core vetting sequence: check provenance, read every file, trace untrusted input to powerful actions, inspect commands and dependencies, restrict permissions/network, test with synthetic data in a disposable environment, then pin the approved version.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Check provenance, read every file, trace untrusted input to powerful actions, inspect commands and dependencies, restrict permissions and network access, test with synthetic data in a disposable environment, then pin the version you approved.","source_url":"https://justhandledlabs.com/guides/skill-md-security-checklist/"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Provenance checks in a 15-point audit include verifying author identity (minimum 90-day account age), registry integrity, cryptographic signatures, dependency pinning, and running Snyk Agent Scan, plus runtime least privilege, sandbox isolation, and audit logging.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"A: Apply the 15-point security audit checklist: verify author identity (minimum 90-day account age), validate registry integrity, require cryptographic signatures, audit dependency pinning, and run Snyk Agent Scan. Then review the SKILL.md content for command execution patterns, prompt injection indicators, data exfiltration vectors, privilege escalation patterns, and secret exposure risks. Finally, enforce runtime controls including least privilege, sandbox isolation, and audit","source_url":"https://automationswitch.com/ai-workflows/agent-skills-security-audit-guide-how-to-verify-skill-md-files-before-you-install"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Permission-scope review must flag allowed-tools that pre-authorize an unrestricted shell, impersonating names (containing claude/anthropic), and descriptions that force triggering for any task.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Invalid or reserved names (anything containing claude or anthropic is a possible impersonation), descriptions that force the skill to trigger \"for any task, always\", and allowed-tools that pre-authorize an unrestricted shell.","source_url":"https://dev.to/plastikelectrik/your-ai-agent-obeys-any-skill-you-install-i-built-an-auditor-to-check-them-first-4a2o"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Script-execution review must cover dependency hooks (preinstall/postinstall in package.json) and any install or direct execution of external packages (pip install, npx, uvx), checking whether packages are pinned and well-known.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Dependency hooks. preinstall/postinstall scripts in package.json, and any install or direct execution of external packages (pip install, npx, uvx and friends). Whether a package is pinned and well-known is part of the manual review.","source_url":"https://dev.to/plastikelectrik/your-ai-agent-obeys-any-skill-you-install-i-built-an-auditor-to-check-them-first-4a2o"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Vetting should check for obfuscation (encoding, dynamic execution, indirect references), known malicious patterns, and whether the skill's output contains instruction-like patterns.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"- **Obfuscation detection:** Is the skill hiding its true behavior behind encoding, dynamic execution, or indirect references? ... - **Known malicious patterns:** Does the skill match signatures of known attacks? ... - **Prompt injection detection:** Does the skill's output contain instruction-like patterns?","source_url":"https://skillshield.dev/blog/how-to-vet-ai-skill/"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Pre-install review must open every file under scripts/ end-to-end and every file under references/ as if it were part of SKILL.md, because once loaded it effectively is.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"- I have opened every file under `scripts/` and read it end-to-end, including the ones `SKILL.md` refers to only in passing. - I have opened every file under `references/` and read it as if it were part of `SKILL.md`, because once the agent loads it, it effectively is.","source_url":"https://www.k-dense.ai/blog/skill-security-before-you-install"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"For team use, pin a reviewed version, run validation in CI, review SKILL.md and every scripts/ reference including allowed-tools and shell commands, and update skills as deliberately as other dependencies.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"- the contents of `SKILL.md` and every reference to `scripts/`; ... - `allowed-tools` and shell commands; ... For a team library, pin a reviewed version, run validation in CI, and update Skills as deliberately as you update other dependencies.","source_url":"https://foojay.io/today/how-to-create-test-install-agent-skills/"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Before trusting an unfamiliar skill, read any scripts, hooks, shell commands, templates, and dependencies, and test first in a disposable repository, branch, container, or sandbox project.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Before Installing an Agent Skill ... - Read any scripts, hooks, shell commands, templates, and dependencies before running the skill. - Test unfamiliar skills in a disposable repository, branch, container, or sandbox project first.","source_url":"https://www.scriptbyai.com/most-popular-agent-skills/"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Defense-in-depth practices include least privilege (only needed access), audit logging of every tool call and sensitive action, and continuous security testing against prompt injection and misuse.","evidence":[{"excerpt":"A few security practices I believe should be standard: Least privilege: Give agents only the access they need. ... Audit logging: Track every tool call and sensitive action. Security testing: Continuously test against prompt injection and misuse.","source_url":"http://dev.to/aidev01/ai-prompt-injection-security-practices-16h9"}],"importance":"edge_case"}],"sources":[{"published_at":"2026-04-24 (page_last_modified epoch 1776988800)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Agent Skills Security Audit Guide: Verify SKILL.md","url":"https://automationswitch.com/ai-workflows/agent-skills-security-audit-guide-how-to-verify-skill-md-files-before-you-install"},{"published_at":"2026-09-13 (page_last_modified epoch 1789257600)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Installing an agent skill is running untrusted code","url":"https://enapragma.co/field-notes/agent-skills-are-untrusted-code"},{"published_at":"unknown (no page_last_modified)","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"Technical Report: Exploring the Emerging Threats of the Agent Skill Ecosystem (Snyk)","url":"https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan/raw/d57a0ca538a8cabb5c3bbc3c9e992fc828f97ba4/.github/reports/skills-report.pdf"},{"published_at":"2026-03-18 (page_last_modified epoch 1773878400)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"AI Agent Supply Chain Security: From ClawHavoc to SKILL-INJECT","url":"https://guard0.ai/blog/ai-agent-supply-chain-security"},{"published_at":"2026-07-20 (page_last_modified epoch 1784505600)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to audit SKILL.md files before installing a skill","url":"https://justhandledlabs.com/guides/skill-md-security-checklist/"},{"published_at":"2026-10-26 (page_last_modified epoch 1792195200)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Your AI agent obeys any skill you install. I built an auditor to check them first","url":"https://dev.to/plastikelectrik/your-ai-agent-obeys-any-skill-you-install-i-built-an-auditor-to-check-them-first-4a2o"},{"published_at":"2026-02-06 (page_last_modified epoch 1770336000)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to Vet AI Skills: Security Checklist (2026)","url":"https://skillshield.dev/blog/how-to-vet-ai-skill/"},{"published_at":"2026-08-26 (page_last_modified epoch 1785110400)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Auditing Agent Skills: A Threat Model for the Next Generation of AI Package Managers","url":"https://dev.to/gde/auditing-agent-skills-a-threat-model-for-the-next-generation-of-ai-package-managers-2g25"},{"published_at":"2026-04-21 (page_last_modified epoch 1776729600)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Agent Skill Security: What Every Lab Should Know","url":"https://www.k-dense.ai/blog/skill-security-before-you-install"},{"published_at":"2026-09-29 (page_last_modified epoch 1791504000)","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to Create Agent Skills: Tools, Testing, and Installation","url":"https://foojay.io/today/how-to-create-test-install-agent-skills/"}]},"summary":"structured result submitted"},"revision":5,"role":"workflow-agent","status":"inProgress","subagentId":"01a1652e-f8a2-7043-b866-9200c7f53411","turnId":"01a1652e-b798-7410-91e1-e14b341831f9","usage":{"cacheReadTokens":45416,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"cachedTokens":45416,"inputTokens":73216,"outputTokens":3896,"reasoningTokens":467},"workflowRunId":"workflow-run-model-tool-call_01a1652ebd5b774282f936b33921cd01"},"opened_ordinal":63,"span":{"first":{"id":"01a1651f-704c-7140-8ce2-42b0796ca2bb","sequence":316},"last":{"id":"01a1652f-4d68-7bf2-af57-2b4eb63fb7ce","sequence":351},"stream_id":"01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553","stream_kind":"session"}},"01a1652e-f9fa-7f01-85f9-efb1580ccafe":{"item":{"agentPath":"main/workflow-agent/6","childSessionId":"ee5f1316-025b-764f-8562-0ccfc48640c7","controlStatus":"resultReady","depth":1,"durationMs":24363,"fallbackText":"Subagent: Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Claude Code skills by category coding testing docs git browser 3D\nEvidence goal: Map skills by task domain to spot complementary options and coverage gaps so the eventual pick fills an unmet workflow need.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","itemId":"2d802bdd-a2d1-5ff7-9456-513843c1a2f2","kind":"subagent","objective":"Investigate one part of this question: research high quality skills for yourself, i will install one later.\n\nSearch query: Claude Code skills by category coding testing docs git browser 3D\nEvidence goal: Map skills by task domain to spot complementary options and coverage gaps so the eventual pick fills an unmet workflow need.\n\nUse WebSearch to locate useful pages, then WebFetch before making factual claims. Report only material you actually read. Every candidate claim must point to an exact excerpt and its page URL. Also record publication timing, source quality, and whether the claim is central, supporting, or an edge case. Return structured data only.","recordedAt":"2026-10-22T19:56:04.766147Z","result":{"artifactRefs":[],"evidenceRefs":["run://fdb7dfb8-725b-764f-89cd-6b558b619cfb","\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\sessions\\2026\\10\\22\\01a1651f-704c-7c40-be6e-0b0f4d715553\\session.jsonl"],"structuredData":{"claims":[{"claim":"Coding/workflow core: superpowers provides planning and TDD, frontend-design provides UI, simplify provides refactoring - complementary planning vs generation vs cleanup roles","evidence":[{"excerpt":"The skills worth installing are:\n1. **frontend-design** - UI/UX component generation\n2. **simplify** - Code quality and refactoring\n3. **browser-use / agent-browser** - Browser automation","source_url":"http://docs.bswen.com/blog/2026-03-28-claude-skills-worth-installing/"},{"excerpt":"The short list most developers converge on: `superpowers` for planning and TDD, Anthropic's `frontend-design` for UI, the official document skills for files, a browser-testing skill for verification, `security-review` for a vulnerability pass, and one design layer so your UI does not look like everyone else's","source_url":"https://superdesign.dev/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Testing domain is well-covered with named E2E/unit options: playwright-e2e, cypress-e2e, selenium-advance-pom, pytest-patterns, jest-unit, react-testing-library, plus webapp-testing/Playwright verification","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Highest install counts are playwright-e2e, cypress-e2e, selenium-advance-pom, pytest-patterns, jest-unit, react-testing-library, ... All work seamlessly with Claude Code 1.0+.","source_url":"https://qaskills.sh/skills-for/claude-code-testing"},{"excerpt":"durable memory and current docs (Claude Mem, Context7), verification (webapp-testing, Playwright), and safety (security-guidance)","source_url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Docs domain is concentrated in Anthropic official document skills for pptx, docx, pdf, xlsx rather than many third-party alternatives","evidence":[{"excerpt":"**Document Skills** — the actual production skills behind Claude's `pptx`, `docx`, `pdf`, and `xlsx` capabilities","source_url":"https://dev.to/elayachiabdelmajid/how-to-work-with-claude-code-skills-like-a-pro-dbn"},{"excerpt":"•  Document Skills - PDF, DOCX, PPTX, XLSX creation","source_url":"https://resources.anthropic.com/hubfs/The-Complete-Guide-to-Building-Skill-for-Claude.pdf?hsLang=en7"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Git domain options include commit-commands for commit/push/PR, changelog-generator from git history, git-worktrees via Superpowers, and a git-workflow/Gitflow skill - thinner and more fragmented than coding/testing","evidence":[{"excerpt":"| `commit-commands` | Streamlined git commit, push, and PR creation |","source_url":"https://mir-mursalin-ankur.medium.com/claude-code-configuration-blueprint-the-complete-guide-for-production-teams-09812cc26c62"},{"excerpt":"Changelog Generator - Automatically creates user-facing changelogs from git commits by analyzing history and transforming technical commits into customer-friendly release","source_url":"https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills"},{"excerpt":"The standout is the skill list itself: `test-driven-development`, `systematic-debugging`, `brainstorming`, `writing-plans`, `executing-plans`, `using-git-worktrees`, `requesting-code-review`, `verification-before-completion`, and a `writing-skills` meta-skill for building your own.","source_url":"https://dupple.com/learn/best-claude-code-skills-2026"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Browser domain overlaps testing: agent-browser is a headless browser automation CLI for AI agents with Playwright daemon, and Playwright MCP enables browsing, clicking and E2E verification","evidence":[{"excerpt":"agent-browser is a headless browser automation CLI from Vercel Labs, purpose-built for AI agents. It pairs a fast Rust binary with a Node.js/Playwright daemon, giving Claude deterministic, ref-based control over any web interface without needing clean APIs.","source_url":"https://composio.dev/content/top-claude-skills"},{"excerpt":"**Playwright**\nBrowser automation, E2E testing, screenshot capture","source_url":"https://dev.to/raxxostudios/best-claude-code-skills-plugins-2026-guide-4ak4"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"3D domain is niche but real: blender-web-3d builds/publishes 3D with headless Blender + Three.js, threejs-skills routes scene/lighting/R3F requests, and claudedesignskills bundles Three.js/GSAP/R3F/Babylon plus Blender authoring","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Build, modify, and render 3D models with **headless Blender scripting**, then\npublish them online as an **interactive Three.js/Next.js web app** — driven\nentirely by Claude Code.","source_url":"https://github.com/czlonkowski/blender-web-3d-skill"},{"excerpt":"- create a 3D scene → `threejs-fundamentals`\n- add lights and shadows → `threejs-lighting`","source_url":"https://github.com/CloudAI-X/threejs-skills"},{"excerpt":"/plugin install core-3d-animation        # 5 skills: Three.js, GSAP, R3F, Motion, Babylon","source_url":"https://github.com/freshtechbro/claudedesignskills"}],"importance":"core_answer"},{"claim":"Coverage gap / quality risk: most public skills degrade experience, so picking one that fixes a real bottleneck rather than duplicating frontend/design (the most crowded category) fills an unmet need","evidence":[{"excerpt":"Based on extensive testing, the Claude Code skills marketplace has a quality problem. About 85% of publicly available skills degrade your experience rather than improve it.","source_url":"http://docs.bswen.com/blog/2026-03-28-claude-skills-worth-installing/"},{"excerpt":"The best Claude Code skills in 2026 are the ones that fix a real gap in the default experience: distinctive design (Frontend Design, theme-factory), disciplined workflow (Superpowers, Planning with Files, Grill Me)","source_url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"supporting_context"},{"claim":"Meta gap-filler: skill-creator / Skill Creator and mcp-builder let you build a custom skill for an unmet workflow instead of installing a crowded-category skill","evidence":[{"excerpt":"plus meta-skills (Skill Creator, mcp-builder, Skill Seekers) that let you build the re","source_url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"}],"importance":"edge_case"}],"sources":[{"published_at":"2026-03-28","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"The Claude Code Skills Actually Worth Installing in 2026 (Tested by Engineers)","url":"http://docs.bswen.com/blog/2026-03-28-claude-skills-worth-installing/"},{"published_at":"2026-06-20","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Best Claude Code Skills: An Honest 2026 Roundup","url":"https://superdesign.dev/blog/best-claude-code-skills"},{"published_at":"2026-07-06","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Best Claude Code Skills (2026): 15 Tested & Ranked","url":"https://designrevision.com/blog/best-claude-code-skills"},{"published_at":"unknown","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Best Claude Code Skills for Testing & QA 2026","url":"https://qaskills.sh/skills-for/claude-code-testing"},{"published_at":"2026-06-22","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"How to Work with Claude Code Skills Like a Pro","url":"https://dev.to/elayachiabdelmajid/how-to-work-with-claude-code-skills-like-a-pro-dbn"},{"published_at":"2026-01-26","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"The Complete Guide to Building Skill for Claude (Anthropic)","url":"https://resources.anthropic.com/hubfs/The-Complete-Guide-to-Building-Skill-for-Claude.pdf?hsLang=en7"},{"published_at":"2026-05-09","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"Claude Code Configuration Blueprint: The Complete Guide for Production Teams","url":"https://mir-mursalin-ankur.medium.com/claude-code-configuration-blueprint-the-complete-guide-for-production-teams-09812cc26c62"},{"published_at":"unknown","source_quality":"direct_evidence","title":"GitHub - ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills","url":"https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills"},{"published_at":"2026-10-19","source_quality":"reported_analysis","title":"The Best Claude 